      <div type="clause" n="23">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ExcomVII">Excom VII</ref> 23</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Excom VII 23" corresp="#wit-cx"><pb n="439" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ealswa þeos candela beoð acwæint fram þisum andweardu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> leohtu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, swa beon heo adwæscede heora sawla ínto helle!</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="439" ed="#liebermann"/>23. Und so wie diese Kerze<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#ExcomVII_23.lnote.de1.a"/> fort von diesen gegenwärtigen Lichtern verlöscht wird, so seien sie, ihre Seelen zur Hölle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#ExcomVII_23.lnote.de1.b"/> vernichtet!</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">23. And just as this candle is extinguished away from these present lights, so may they, their souls, be destroyed into hell!</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text and German translation transcribed from Gesetze I p. 439 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="ExcomVII_23.lnote.de1.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">439</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> I 14</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> I 14</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="ExcomVII_23.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">439</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. o.</hi> 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf. above</hi> 5</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
